BEGIN_TEXT
This box sends and receives MARS traffic with no shell and no settings
file. Everything goes in through forms, and every screen has its own page
in this guide: press ? on any screen.

Seven steps take a box from the can to its first message. The box ticks
each one off as it sees it done, so you can stop and come back.

 1. Give the box your call.
 2. Show your card to your keymaster.
 3. Choose whose authority you take.
 4. Enter your channels.
 5. Know when your nets meet.
 6. Load your key tape.
 7. Send your first message.

The choice of keymaster is yours alone. Nothing on the box, in a bundle or
in a handout picks one for you.

Not sure yet? Turn on training. It loads sample traffic into a separate
practice store, so you can try every screen. Nothing you do in training
goes on the air, and none of it mixes with your real traffic.
END
BEGIN_EXAMPLE
A member opens a sealed box after an outage. The box asks for the call
(step 1). At the rally point net control reads its fingerprint aloud; the
member checks it and accepts net control as keymaster (steps 2 and 3).
Net control's startup bundle brings channels and schedules (4 and 5), the
sealed tape comes over the air (6), and the member sends a check-in (7).
END
